se,"integrationCompulsory":false,"postGraduateDegreeType":null}}]}],"rowCount":38,"completeModules":true,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-31T16:43:47Z","programNotes":[{"title":"学科专业简介","text":"The program is dedicated to cultivating globally competitive composite talents through all-English lectures. The program features an international curriculum and cross-cultural academic exchanges, enabling students to master cutting-edge technologies in data science and at the same time have the ability to collaborate and innovate in a multicultural environment. The program focuses on the cross-fertilization of computational mathematics, statistics, computer science and industrial applications, and encourages students to participate in international scientific research cooperation and industrial practice, aiming to create a group of composite big data talents who are proficient in professional technology, have interdisciplinary innovation ability and international vision."},{"title":"培养目标","text":"This program cultivates “composite” talents with all-round development in morality, intelligence, physicality,&nbsp; and aesthetics, good political quality and moral cultivation, who are able to engage in the teaching, scientific research, development and application of big data by using the basic theories, methods and skills of data modeling, analysis and processing, and statistical inference."},{"title":"基本要求","text":"This program requires students to master the basic knowledge of statistics, computer, mathematics and applied disciplines related to big data, as well as the basic skills of data analysis, technology development and application. Through systematic study of specialized courses, the program aims to cultivate data science talents and data technology talents who have both strict professional and technical training and profound data vision, and to meet the demand for basic talents in big data-related industries."},{"title":"修业要求","text":"\n\n\n\n1.Years of study：4 years（Bachelor）2.Degree Conferment Instructions：\n\n\n\n\nDegree\n\n\nMajor\n\n\nRequirements\n\n\n\n\nBachelor of Science\n\n\nData Science and Big Data Technology\n\n\n■ No fewer than 126 credits\n\n\n\n\n■ Course Requirement\n\n\nGeneral Education Courses&nbsp; 26 credits\n\n\n\n\nMajor Courses 63 credits\n\n\n\n\nRegular Major Track 30 credits\n\n\n\n\nIntegrated Innovation Courses 7 credits\n\n\n\n"},{"title":"学分要求","text":"Regular Major Track (126 Credits)Students in this program are required to complete a total of 126 credits, including no less than 31.5 practical credits, at least 2 aesthetic education credits (with a minimum of 1 credit from either \"Aesthetics and Art History\" or \"Art Appreciation and Criticism\" courses, plus participation in at least one art practice activity), and no fewer than 32 labor education hours while meeting the Labor Week requirements. The credit distribution consists of 26 general education credits, 59 core professional training credits, 24 advanced specialization module credits, and 7 integrated innovation capability module credits."},{"title":"学位要求","text":"Bachelor's DegreeStudents who meet the following requirements by the end of their fourth year will be awarded a Bachelor of Science degree.（1）Completion of all required credits and fulfillment of all stipulations specified in the undergraduate program curriculum;（2）Achievement of a minimum cumulative GPA of 2.0 or above, calculated based on all valid course grades as stipulated by the program curriculum in effect at the time of graduation."},{"title":"课程体系与科研训练体系","text":""}]}